SUMMARY:Urban Trees in a Changing Climate
DESCRIPTION:Join a conversation with Lancaster City’s Urban Foresters and conservationists for a discussion about the benefits of a healthy treed city and neighborhoods\, as well as the challenges the City and homeowners face with excessive heat and extreme weather events. Light refreshments will be provided.  \n\n\n\nProgram Topics: – Why urban trees are so important – Recent storms and the impact on trees and residents – City of Lancaster and Tree Tender tree programs – The Street Tree Arboretum at Buchanan Park as a resource – i-Tree Tools programs and apps – Basic tree maintenance and preventative care for tree health and resiliency  \n\n\n\n\n    Learn More
URL:https://figlancaster.com/event/urban-trees-in-a-changing-climate/
LOCATION:Buchanan Park Picnic Pavilion and Street Tree Arboretum\, 901 Buchanan Ave\, Lancaster\, PA\, 17603\, United States
CATEGORIES:Education & Classes
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://fig.guide/content/uploads/sites/3/2026/08/URBAN-TREES-v8.13-1-1-2-3-1.avif
ORGANIZER;CN="College Park Climate Action Neighborhood":MAILTO:CollegeParkCAN@gmail.com
END:VEVENT
